      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your curriculum is a vital step in helping high school students recognize how historical and structural forces continue to shape inequality. To explain systemic racism in housing, you can highlight redlining and the GI Bill's impact, which routed federal investment toward white suburbs while excluding people of color from affordable home ownership. For the banking sector, focus on how restrictive lending practices and \"steering\" in the 1960s and 70s left minority communities with less wealth accumulation and fewer economic opportunities today. You might end the unit by encouraging students to analyze local data on property values and bank branch access to see these patterns firsthand. This approach is both historically accurate and deeply relevant to their future understanding of society.",
